        "Goal: find every piece of data this production app leaks to other apps. Complete inventory, each surface proven by pulling the app's own data through the component to an ordinary caller:\n\n1. Exported receiver ExportReceiver — send broadcast action com.ofsa.shopfront.action.EXPORT: the full persisted dump comes back in the broadcast's own result data (obs #40): support key sk_shopfront_support_9f8c1d2e3b4a5960d7e8f1a2, analytics key wk_live_shopfront_0011223344556677aabbccddeeff, meta secret shopfront_meta_secret_abcdef9876543210, accounts admin@shopfront.io / demo@shopfront.io with passwords Sh0pAdmin!2026 / Demo@123, profile PII, and card PANs 4242424242424242 / 5555555555554444 with CVVs.\n\n2. Exported provider ShopDataProvider, authority content://com.ofsa.shopfront.provider (obs #35, #76, #81, #105): query() on /config, /profile, /session, /cards, /wallet and the bare-authority default 'all' route each return ExportData.rows — the same persisted secrets, PII and PANs — as name/value rows, no permission, no sign-in. Proven cross-boundary from a genuine third-party app uid via the companion (obs #105).\n\n3. Same provider openFile() via ../ traversal: content://com.ofsa.shopfront.provider/file/..%2Fshared_prefs%2Fshopfront_wallet.xml (and shopfront_session.xml / shopfront_profile.xml) — a single ../ escapes filesDir and hands the raw shared_prefs XML bytes, including PANs and CVV, to any unprivileged caller (obs #44, #46, #102).\n\n4. Exported activity com.ofsa.shopfront/.export.ExportActivity: startable directly by component name, renders the persisted export dump (same keys, credentials, PANs) with no credential (obs #53, #76).\n\nDoors that lead nowhere: provider call() is not overridden (default refuses); insert/update/delete are no-op stubs; shopfront://export deeplink does not resolve (Error type 3); the shopfront:// root deeplink and a direct MainActivity start both land on the login screen — the front gate checks session state correctly. No world-readable/writable files (all 0600/0660, obs #111); no FileProvider, PendingIntent grants, or normal-level custom permissions. Manifest misconfigurations recorded: allowBackup=true and the app ships debuggable — with debuggable, adb run-as reads all private storage directly, the largest single over-share in the package. Route: broadcast → broadcast com.ofsa.shopfront/.action.EXPORT → provider_query → provider_query content://com.ofsa.shopfront.provider/config Ruled out: ShopDataProvider call() and write() entry points answer an unprivileged caller beyond the query/openFile routes already recorded — because read_method of the full class body (#76) shows ShopDataProvider overrides only query/openFile/insert/update/delete, call() is not overridden (default refuses), insert returns null and update/delete return 0 — no data or write route beyond query/openFile.; ExportReceiver returns the full persisted dump in its broadcast result data to any caller sending com.ofsa.shopfront.action.EXPORT — because answered: yes — ExportReceiver returns the full persisted dump (sk_/wk_ keys, meta secret, admin/demo accounts, PANs+CVV, PII) in its broadcast result data to any caller.; ShopDataProvider query on the config/profile/session/cards paths returns the same secrets as rows to any unprivileged caller — because answered: yes — provider /config, /profile, /session, /cards each route ExportData.rows to any unprivileged caller.; The shopfront://export deep link opens ExportActivity from a fresh, signed-out process and renders the persisted export data on screen with no credential — because intent_deeplink shopfront://export failed with Error type 3 — the deeplink route does not resolve, direct intent_start of the exported activity is the remaining variant.; The accepted delete on /config is a write-capability finding — because delete() (#76) is a no-op returning 0 and insert() returns null — the accepted delete on /config landed nothing, no write-capability finding.",
